    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/RegisUniversity/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Associate-Assistant-Professor-Physical-Therapy_R005442": {
      "title": "Associate/Assistant Professor-Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-13\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: The School of Rehabilitative and Health Sciences (SRHS) in the Rueckert-Hartman College for Health Professions at Regis University seeks applicants for a 12-month faculty appointment at the rank of assistant or associate professor. Responsibilities include teaching in assigned areas of expertise, scholarship, student advising, and service at all levels of the University. Regis University School of Rehabilitative and Health Sciences is committed to health justice, inclusion and diverse perspectives among its faculty and students. We are currently seeking faculty applicants who resonate with the university mission. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Each faculty member is expected to be collegial, adhere to the School Workplace Commitment, participate in shared governance at the School, College, and/or University level, and be an engaged citizen of the University through participation in the functional and ceremonial life of the institution.  Ranked faculty members participate in teaching, student advising, scholarship, service, and as appropriate, clinical practice. Teaching is a major responsibility of the faculty, and this encompasses course development, organization, selection of assignments and preparation for class, assessment activities including testing, timely notification of student progress, and assistance for individual students. In addition to individual course preparation, the faculty regularly participate in overall curriculum evaluation and revision according to changes and trends in the field of physical therapy, health care, and education. The faculty participate actively in student advising for the academic welfare and professional development of the students. This involves meeting(s), electronic and personal communication with advisee students each semester. Faculty are expected to be active in scholarly endeavors which contribute to the professional body of knowledge. The hallmark of scholarly activities is the process of peer-review and dissemination. Faculty members are assigned committee duties necessary to maintain and improve University, College, School/Program operations and outcomes. Faculty members who are teaching clinical content in the curriculum are strongly encouraged to seek clinical practice opportunities to maintain clinical competency and remain informed regarding contemporary physical therapist practice. Faculty attendance is expected at University Commencement, All-School Meetings (ASMs), SRHS All-day meetings (RLMs), and Provost Faculty Workshop (August). Additionally, DPT faculty are expected to attend SRHS specific ceremonies. Qualified faculty candidates must have: •    A current physical therapist license and be in good standing with their state's professional practice division. •    A terminal academic doctoral degree in a related field from an accredited institution preferred OR a clinical doctoral degree. Evidence of advanced clinical certification such as ABPTS specialization in Cardiopulmonary (CCS)or Pediatrics (PCS).  •    Teaching experience in physical therapy, evidence of scholarship dissemination (peer-reviewed publication or presentation), and demonstrated commitment to inclusive practices in teaching, scholarship, and service. Special knowledge, skills, abilities General Ability to think creatively and critically, define problems, gather and establish facts, draw valid conclusions, and develop solutions and propose appropriate courses of action  Demonstrate ethical and professional behavior consistent with the mission of Regis University  Strong understanding of technology for use, at minimum, for teaching, learning and student assessment.  Teaching experience in physical therapy, health science or exercise science  Evidence of scholarship dissemination (peer-reviewed publication or presentation)   Demonstrated commitment to inclusive practices in teaching, scholarship, practice and/or service  Skills: (Psychomotor activities needed to perform tasks)  Demonstrated skill in teaching and learning theories, instructional principles and practices, and curriculum design  Leadership and team building skills  Outstanding oral and written communication skills  Demonstrated organizational skills  Project planning and priority setting capabilities  Knowledge: (Body of and level of information necessary to perform a duty)  Knowledge of the art and science of physical therapy and the essentials of doctoral-level education   Knowledge of health science and/or exercise science and the essentials of health and exercises science baccalaureate education  Demonstrated knowledge in teaching and learning theories, instructional principles and practices, and curriculum design  Abilities: (Application of knowledge, i.e., intensity, duration, frequency of mental capabilities needed to perform tasks)  Teach using a variety of teaching modalities  Develop and/or modify course structure and content for given student populations and learning environments   Evaluate course delivery  Advise students  Mentor faculty  Use Microsoft Windows, Microsoft Office, Web-browser, personal information management software, advising, and information management software  Work to deadline  Physical and Mental Aspects: (Frequency, duration, very easy to hard, essential to helpful)  Lifting & Carrying: Occasional lifting and carrying – essential   Pushing & Pulling: Access files and other materials – routine  Body Positions: Sits at specific desk – frequently  Stands at presentations – frequently  Body Movements: Requires stooping and reaching – frequently  Hand Use: Able to use keyboard, computer, copier, fax, phone, and other standard office equipment; Specific courses may have additional requirements  Location:  May require travel to other sites or off campus visits;  Telecommuting: Available as workload and staffing permit  Sense of Touch: Able to use computer and office equipment, communicate in person, and write; Specific courses may have additional requirements  Hearing: Able to communicate in person and on all audio devices; Specific courses may have additional requirements  Vision: Able to use computer and office equipment; observe people; write and read a variety of printed, handwritten, and digital materials; evaluate written, printed and digital materials; drive a car  Mental: Mathematics (Counting, adding, subtracting etc.)  Use a standard calculator, calculate percentages, basic understanding of budgeting, statistics, data, graphs, charts, and other data represented numerically    Ability to recall procedures and policies  Language Ability: (Reading, writing, speaking)   Strong oral and written communication skills required  Reasoning: (Judgment and decision making)   Critical thinking and strong decision-making skills essential  Other requirements: Must be able to travel by car and by airplane  This is a Full time (1.0 FTE) position. Ranked faculty are hired on FTE Faculty Contracts.  Holiday and leave vary according to FTE.  All leave (unpaid, professional, and service) is planned with the School in order to ensure effective year-round operation of the School’s education programs. Faculty are expected to be available during the workday 8am-5pm and on campus (vs. remote) 3/5 days per week. Instructions to Applicants:  Please submit a resume, cover letter and list of references with your application. Current employees, please submit an application by logging into Workday. Click on the Career Worklet and access the internal site. This position will remain posted until filled, with a preferred application deadline of November 1, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration. Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission Leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: $88,000-$99,360/ annually, commensurate with qualifications Application Deadline: Post Internally and Externally"
    },
    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/RegisUniversity/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Secondary-Education--Tenure-Track-_R005457": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Secondary Education (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: The Division of Education at Regis University invites applications for a full-time, tenure track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, beginning August 2027. This position is dedicated to on-ground, traditional (in-person) undergraduate teaching within our education program. The Department is engaged in a significant curricular redesign initiative. The faculty member in this role will serve as a core member of the design team, contributing directly to the development of the revised program. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar to teach courses in foundations of education, and secondary content, methods, and assessment, as well as courses focused on culturally and linguistically diverse (CLD) learners, while contributing to program development, advising, and service. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities • Teach on-ground, in-person undergraduate courses in the teacher preparation program, including foundations, secondary content-area, methods, and assessment courses, as well as a course focused on culturally and linguistically  diverse learners • Maintain regular on-campus presence for classes, office hours, advising, and meetings • Advise undergraduate education majors • Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to rank • Participate in divisional, college, and university service • Support program accreditation and continuous improvement effort • Serve on the Committee on Teacher Education at Regis and act as the primary point of contact for majors connected to Secondary Education. About the Division of Education at Regis University The Division of Education at Regis University prepares educators and leaders through both traditional and post-traditional pathways. On the undergraduate side, we offer traditional on-ground coursework leading to initial teacher licensure, with a strong emphasis on face to-face instruction and field-based experience. The Division also serves post-traditional and graduate students through online offerings, including a range of graduate and licensure programs. Across all programs, our faculty are committed to preparing licensed, classroom-ready educators and leaders equipped to serve diverse K–12 populations. The Division of Education is part of Regis College, the traditional liberal arts college of Regis University, which is a Hispanic Serving Institution, serving approximately 2000 traditional undergraduate students (~60% of whom are students of color; ~30% of whom are first generation college students). Required Qualifications • Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Education, Curriculum & Instruction, Teacher Education, or a closely related field completed by [start date] • Demonstrated ability or experience teaching traditional, on-ground undergraduate courses in foundations and assessment of education and secondary instruction, teaching methods, and assessment • Demonstrated expertise or experience related to culturally and linguistically diverse learners, multicultural education, or instruction for Multilingual Learners (ML/ELL). • Evidence of effective face-to-face undergraduate teaching • Commitment to preparing pre-service teachers for diverse K–12 classrooms • Record of (or potential for) scholarship, presentations, or publications in teacher education • K–12 classroom teaching experience Preferred Qualifications • Experience with curriculum design and accreditation processes • Professional development, mentoring, and/or instructional coaching experience • Bilingual or multilingual proficiency  • Demonstrated success at a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI) or similar experience with an institution or program focused on fostering success of students of color  Instructions to Applicants: Please submit the following documents with your application: Letter of interest addressing qualifications above/Cover Letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research, including evidence of research productivity or potential In addition, please send three letters of recommendation, at least one of which addresses the candidate’s demonstrated abilities and/or potential as an undergraduate teacher and mentor, directly to Jami Thompson at jthompson027@regis.edu . Questions may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Rona McCall at rmccall@regis.edu . Current employees, please submit an application by logging into Workday. Click on the Career Worklet and access the internal site. This position will remain posted until filled, with a preferred application deadline of October 12, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration. Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission Leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: $60,000-64,000/ annually commensurate with qualifications Application Deadline:"
    },
    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/RegisUniversity/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Elementary-Education--Tenure-Track-_R005458": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Elementary Education (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: The Division of Education at Regis University invites applications for a full-time, tenuretrack faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, beginning August 2027. This position is dedicated to on-ground, traditional (in-person) undergraduate teaching within our education program. The Department is engaged in a significant curricular redesign initiative. The faculty member in this role will serve as a core member of the design team, contributing directly to the development of the revised program. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar to teach courses in foundations of education, and elementary reading or mathematics content, methods, and assessment, as well as courses focused on culturally and linguistically diverse (CLD) learners, while contributing to program development, advising, and service. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities • Teach on-ground, in-person undergraduate courses in the teacher preparation program, including foundations, assessment, and elementary reading or mathematic content-area, methods, and assessment courses, as well as a course focused on culturally and linguistically diverse learners • Maintain regular on-campus presence for classes, office hours, advising, and meetings • Advise undergraduate education majors • Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to rank • Participate in divisional, college, and university service • Support program accreditation and continuous improvement effort • Serve on the Committee on Teacher Education at Regis and act as the primary point of contact for the on-ground Elementary Education program. About the Division of Education at Regis University The Division of Education at Regis University prepares educators and leaders through both traditional and post-traditional pathways. On the undergraduate side, we offer traditional on-ground coursework leading to initial teacher licensure, with a strong emphasis on face to-face instruction and field-based experience. The Division also serves post-traditional and graduate students through online offerings, including a range of graduate and licensure programs. Across all programs, our faculty are committed to preparing licensed, classroom-ready educators and leaders equipped to serve diverse K–12 populations. The Division of Education is part of Regis College, the traditional liberal arts college of Regis University, which is a Hispanic Serving Institution, serving approximately 2000 traditional undergraduate students (~60% of whom are students of color; ~30% of whom are first generation college students). Required Qualifications • Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Education, Curriculum & Instruction, Teacher Education, or a closely related field completed by start date. • Demonstrated ability or experience teaching traditional, on-ground undergraduate courses in foundations and assessment of education and elementary reading or mathematics instruction, teaching methods, and assessment • Demonstrated expertise or experience related to culturally and linguistically diverse learners, multicultural education, or instruction for Multilingual Learners (ML/ELL). • Evidence of effective face-to-face undergraduate teaching • Commitment to preparing pre-service teachers for diverse K–12 classrooms • Record of (or potential for) scholarship, presentations, or publications in teacher education • K–12 classroom teaching experience Preferred Qualifications • Experience with curriculum design and accreditation processes • Strong literacy/reading background, to include Science of Reading training. • Professional development, mentoring, and/or instructional coaching experience • Bilingual or multilingual proficiency  • Demonstrated success at a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI) or similar experience with an institution or program focused on fostering success of students of color  Instructions to Applicants: Please submit the following documents with your application: Letter of interest addressing qualifications above/Cover Letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research, including evidence of research productivity or potential In addition, please send three letters of recommendation, at least one of which addresses the candidate’s demonstrated abilities and/or potential as an undergraduate teacher and mentor, directly to Jami Thompson at jthompson027@regis.edu . Questions may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Rona McCall at rmccall@regis.edu . Current employees, please submit an application by logging into Workday. Click on the Career Worklet and access the internal site. This position will remain posted until filled, with a preferred application deadline of October 12, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration. Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission Leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: $60,000-$64,000/ annually, commensurate with qualifications Application Deadline:"
    },
    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/RegisUniversity/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Lecturer--Marketing_R005462": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: The Anderson College of Business and Computing at Regis University in Denver, Colorado invites applications for a Lecturer of Marketing (full-time) to begin in Fall of 2027. Qualified candidates will have an MBA, Master’s Degree in Marketing, or a PhD in Marketing or a doctorate in a related field and will show potential for excellent teaching. Applicants should have experience working in a marketing-related field, and successful candidates will be expected to maintain some form of practice in order to maintain their currency in the discipline while teaching. Applicants with knowledge and experience in the areas of digital marketing, advertising and promotion, and/or international marketing are preferred. Major Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to teach about nine graduate and/or undergraduate classes in their discipline based on the needs of various programs. The modalities may vary—in-person, online asynchronous, or hybrid—depending on the course, but it is expected that the candidate will primarily teach on campus. Maintain currency in the field of marketing through industry practice (e.g., consulting projects, work in industry) and/or scholarship (e.g., research publications, presenting at conferences). Conduct service to the department and college as a participating faculty member (e.g., hold office hours, write letters of recommendation for students, attend department meetings, serve on committees, etc.). Advise students around course registration needs. Minimum Qualifications A graduate degree in marketing or a related field Ability to design, develop, and teach marketing courses Demonstrated potential to contribute to academic life beyond the classroom Ability to teach digital marketing, advertising and promotion, and/or international marketing preferred This position will remain posted until filled, with a preferred application deadline of October 23, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a CV/resume, cover letter, teaching statement, and list of references with your application. Current employees, please submit an application and requested documents by logging into Workday. Click on the Career Worklet to access the internal jobs site. Background and Context The Anderson College of Business and Computing was founded in 2020 to prepare students for a complex and ever-changing world that is increasingly blending business and technology. Founded on systems thinking, the College’s innovative curriculum develops graduates who are omni-skilled, resilient, and ready to contribute to a more flourishing world. At Regis University, we affirm our commitment to cultivating an inclusive, welcoming community grounded in Jesuit values and respect for the dignity of every person. Guided by cura personalis , we honor the whole person and recognize that our shared life is enriched by diverse perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. In the spirit of the Universal Apostolic Preferences, we strive to walk with those who are marginalized, journey alongside students and colleagues in formation, and act with care for our common home. We seek individuals who are committed to justice, dialogue, and mutual respect, and who will contribute to a community rooted in belonging, compassion, and the common good. For more information regarding the position please contact: Matt Daly, Associate Dean, Professor of Accounting mdaly@regis.edu or Abby Schneider, Ph.D., Professor and Program Director of Marketing aschneider@regis.edu Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission Leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: $50,000.00/annually Application Deadline: Post Internally and Externally"
    }
  },
